   "file": "content/FMA_13329/tier1.md",
   "text": "Each axillary vein carries blood from the arm back toward the heart. It receives blood from the cephalic vein, which drains the surface of the arm. It then passes through the body wall and becomes the subclavian vein, which lies deep in the chest.",
